        "facts": ["The returning prisoner sees badly in the dark and is mocked.", "Socrates suggests the prisoners might kill whoever tried to free them, recalling Socrates' execution.", "Plato says philosophers must be compelled to rule, and that reluctant rulers rule best.", "A strong answer considers whether the duty is owed to the city, to the prisoners, or to justice itself."],
