        "facts": ["Plato argues only those who know the Good know what truly benefits the city.", "Critics such as Karl Popper read this as a warrant for authoritarian rule.", "A strong answer asks who decides who has seen the light and how errors are checked.", "It distinguishes expertise in a field from authority over others' lives."],
        "misconceptions": ["Plato was arguing for democracy.", "If someone knows better, they automatically have the right to rule."] }
