      "When anomalies pile up, a crisis can lead to a revolution, as when Copernican astronomy replaced the Ptolemaic system or Lavoisier's chemistry replaced phlogiston theory. Kuhn argued that rival paradigms are partly incommensurable: they use terms differently and value different problems, so the switch cannot be settled by a simple neutral test and resembles a conversion or gestalt switch.",
      "Each view has critics. Popper's opponents note that scientists rightly hold on to theories in the face of anomalies; Newton's theory seemed refuted by the orbit of Uranus until the anomaly led to the discovery of Neptune. Any test also relies on auxiliary assumptions, so a failed prediction does not show which belief is false. Kuhn's critics, including Popper and Imre Lakatos, charged that he made theory change a matter of \"mob psychology\" rather than reason; Kuhn replied that shared values such as accuracy, consistency, scope, simplicity and fruitfulness guide choice without dictating it. Lakatos proposed research programmes with a protected hard core as a middle way.",
